<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- SpotBugs project decisions: a rule, or a rule in part of the code, that the team has decided not
     to enforce. One Match per decision, with a comment giving the reason, for example:

       <!- - JPA entities share associations by design (reason ...) - ->
       <Match><Package name="~team\.projectpulse\..*"/><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP"/></Match>

     Unlike the baseline, this file may grow, but every entry is a reviewed decision. -->
<FindBugsFilter>
  <!-- D1 (triage slice 8): EI_EXPOSE_REP / EI_EXPOSE_REP2 off project-wide.
       The 219 baselined findings fall in three kinds of class, and none is a defect here:
       - JPA entities (Course, Section, Team, Student, ...) return and accept their associations.
         Hibernate tracks the exact collection and entity instances it loaded; returning or storing
         a copy would break dirty checking, lazy loading, and orphanRemoval.
       - Spring beans (controllers, services, authorization managers) store constructor-injected
         singletons. Copying an injected bean is meaningless.
       - DTOs and records built per request and serialized once by Jackson; no caller keeps or
         shares them, so an aliased List cannot be mutated behind anyone's back.
       SpotBugs filters cannot match by annotation, so this cannot be narrowed to "entities and beans"
       without a fragile list of class names. Revisit if a long-lived, shared value object appears. -->
  <Match><Bug pattern="EI_EXPOSE_REP,EI_EXPOSE_REP2"/></Match>
</FindBugsFilter>
